---
description: Require a pull request for each completed project change
alwaysApply: true
---

# Pull request workflow

- For any task that changes project files, work on a focused branch based on the latest `main`; do not commit directly to `main`.
- Finish the task by pushing the branch and opening a pull request targeting `main`. Keep the PR limited to the task and exclude unrelated or in-progress work from other branches or agents.
- Before opening the PR, review its diff and run the relevant project checks. Include the checks and their results in the PR description; state clearly when a check was skipped or blocked.
- Do not merge the PR unless the user explicitly asks. Provide the PR link and a concise summary when handing the task back.
- Read-only tasks or tasks that produce no project-file changes do not need a PR. If pushing or opening a PR is blocked, explain the blocker and leave the task marked incomplete.
